  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia RP activist camp</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 4-day regional camp will bring together 20 youth leaders and climate justice activists from across Asia, including Timor-Leste, Indonesia, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Pakistan, India, and Bangladesh. These youth, aged 18&#x2013;30, represent youth-led movements and organizations working on climate advocacy, organizing, and storytelling.As one of the most climate-vulnerable regions, Asia faces disproportionate impacts of the climate crisis. In light of the upcoming COP30, this camp aims to strengthen regional youth capacities, amplifyfrontline experiences, and co-develop a collective campaign for climate justice and finance accountability.Participants will engagein thematic sessions on climate justice, demystifying climate finance, and regional power dynamics. Theywill co-create an Asia Youth Position on Climate Finance, visit climate-affected communities in Bangladesh, produce multimedia content to amplify local voices,and plan coordinated mobilizations in the lead-up to COP30.The camp will culminate in a high-visibility collective action and pressconference in Dhaka, drawing regional media and public attention to youth-led demands. Expected outcomes include a regional youth climate finance position brief, a COP30 youth mobilization strategy, and enhanced solidarity across borders.</narrative>
  </description>
